<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady against poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady against poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday with arrivals lower due to overcast skies in producing areas, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm and demand good on limited supply from plants and refineries with prices rising by 300 rupese per tonne. Business volumes were good and the undertone firm.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady but there was little trade. Soymeal yellow was $270-271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $127-128 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,400 rupees per tonne FOR Bedibunder and was 4,350-4,375 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Business volumes were low.</p>
